# Rocky Linux 9.8 "Blue Onyx". Captured 2026-08-17 from the official image on Docker Hub:
# docker run --rm rockylinux/rockylinux:9 cat /etc/os-release, image digest
# sha256:8101994123cf3d0a8fee517bee7f39e555c7d92bd2d9eb3303cc988a0eeed00f. The same container's
# /etc/redhat-release reads "Rocky Linux release 9.8 (Blue Onyx)", which is what makes Ansible answer
# distribution Rocky: it reads the first word of that file, and Rocky is in the RedHat family list in
# OS_FAMILY_MAP. So this fixture proves the first branch of the derivation, not the ID_LIKE one.
